{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 Map last touched track MIDI to OMNI\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Disable "Map input to channel" (set to omnichannel / -1) on the last-touched track\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 Move all note events of selected MIDI items to channel 1\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 This script moves all note events inside the selected MIDI items to channel 1.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Script logic\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Iterate over selected items, select all note events, move them to channel 1 (right click -> Note Channel -> 1)\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 Name-match import files as new active takes for selected items\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Matches selected media items to user-picked audio files by a shared core key (cue number + instrument number, e.g. "1m03_01"), then inserts each matched audio file as a new active take on the corresponding item.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 Matching logic\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Core key pattern: "%d+m%d+_%d+" (e.g. "1m03_01")\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab The key is searched inside the basename of both the item's active take source filename and each picked audio file. Project prefixes and render suffixes are ignored automatically.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Example: "1m03_01_Drums_pre-comb" matches "WOUI_1m03_01_Drums_comb"\sa180\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 Route selected tracks to new bus track\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Creates a new Bus track and routes all currently selected tracks to it via sends.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Disables the selected tracks' Master/Parent send so audio flows through the Bus to Master.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Prompts for Bus track name\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Prompts for placement: after last selected track OR at end of project\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Prompts whether to prefix name with "B" (checkbox, default ON)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Sets Bus track's channel count to the maximum channel count found among selected tracks\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Creates sends from each selected track to the Bus track, sending all source channels\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 Notes on multichannel audio for script development\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Reaper send channel mapping: you can set source/dest channel via B_MUTE and I_SRCCHAN/I_DSTCHAN fields. For multichannel, set I_SRCCHAN = -1 to send "all channels" (Reaper uses -1 for automatic/all). Alternatively, we can set the destination track to have the appropriate number of channels and leave default mapping.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 Route selected tracks to new send FX track\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Creates a new FX "bus" track and routes all currently selected tracks to it.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Prompts for FX track name\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Prompts for placement: after last selected track OR at end of project\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Prompts whether to prefix name with "FX" (checkbox, default ON)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Sets FX track's channel count to the maximum channel count found among selected tracks\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Creates sends from each selected track to the FX track, sending all source channels\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 Notes on multichannel audio for script development\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Reaper send channel mapping: you can set source/dest channel via B_MUTE and I_SRCCHAN/I_DSTCHAN fields. For multichannel, set I_SRCCHAN = -1 to send "all channels" (Reaper uses -1 for automatic/all). Alternatively, we can set the destination track to have the appropriate number of channels and leave default mapping.\par}
}

